  "description": "AFOKEL crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C40 H90 Ce3 N1 O13,C6 H14. From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 3 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.683-3.728 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.03-102.82°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C40H90Ce3NO13·C6H14. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
